  <prompt>Scope the FR-03 per-Action bounded grounded-tool allow-list onto the sanctioned deterministic pre-filter so that, for an advisory capability's turn, ONLY its declared allow-listed grounded tools mount. Express this as DETERMINISTIC PRE-FILTER narrowing in `AgentToolProjection.PreFilter` (~:123–187) + `AgentToolCatalogProjector` (~:74–433) — a context-scoping predicate keyed off the Action's allow-list. The single Text-path agent turn MUST remain the sole probabilistic decider: add NO classifier, NO second intent-detection, NO routing surface. Verify against ADR-039 MUST-NOTs.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Deep familiarity with the ADR-039 deterministic tool-projection / PreFilter path and the closed-catalog invariant (one decider, pre-filter is the only aid).</role>
  <goal>For an advisory capability's turn, only its declared allow-listed grounded tools mount (via the deterministic pre-filter); the single Text-path agent turn stays the sole decider; no classifier / second dispatch surface is added.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-02 — advisory mode + bounded allow-list on the one decider. ADR-039 permits exactly ONE probabilistic decider (the Text-path agent turn) and FORBIDS any new capability-selecting surface. So the bounded tool set from FR-03 (task 010) MUST be expressed as DETERMINISTIC PRE-FILTER narrowing — a context-scoping predicate in `AgentToolProjection.PreFilter` (~:123–187) + `AgentToolCatalogProjector` (~:74–433) — NOT a new executor, classifier, or routing config. The 2026-07-25 ADR-039 amendment added `output_determinism: fact|advisory`; `advisory` sanctions grounded reasoning + recommendations with every fact cited. This task narrows the mounted tool set to the Action's allow-list when the capability is advisory; task 010 supplies the per-Action opt-in, task 012 authors the advisory Action that opts in to {grid_overview, daily_briefing_overview}. redesign-r2 is CLOSED so Services/Ai is editable by R4 — still keep AI-facade discipline (ADR-013) and /conflict-check with assistant-r3 + compose-r5/r6 on the shared projection files.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AgentToolProjection.cs (PreFilter ~:123–187 — add the allow-list narrowing predicate here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AgentToolCatalogProjector.cs (~:74–433 — the catalog projection that mounts tools)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/AnalysisActionService.cs (the FR-03 opt-in from task 010 — source of the allow-list)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md (the MUST-NOTs to verify against: one decider; no classifier; no routing outside the Binding table)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (projection unit tests with/without allow-list — NFR-08)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039" scope="the pre-filter narrowing predicate">The bounded allow-list is deterministic pre-filtering ONLY; MUST NOT add a classifier, a second intent-detection, or any routing config outside the Binding table; the single Text-path agent turn MUST remain the sole probabilistic decider. Advisory factual claims elsewhere MUST be cited — the projection MUST NOT loosen that.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013" scope="Services/Ai placement">Preserve the AI-facade discipline; do NOT inject AI-internal types into CRUD code even though Services/Ai is R4-editable (redesign-r2 closed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project" scope="scoping expression">The allow-list narrowing MUST be a context-scoping predicate on the existing PreFilter — MUST NOT be a new executor or dispatch surface (§11 reuse-first / NFR-06 / NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="BFF §10" scope="every BFF-touching change">Publish size ≤60 MB compressed (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs) — measure and report absolute + delta; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08" scope="the projection change">Add/update unit tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (projection with/without the allow-list).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
