      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the FR-03 opt-in from task 010 (the per-Action bounded-tool allow-list on `AnalysisAction`) and the current PreFilter / catalog projector flow.</step>
    <step order="2">In `AgentToolProjection.PreFilter` (~:123–187) add a predicate that narrows the mounted tool set to the Action's allow-list when the capability is advisory (deterministic context scoping — no intent detection).</step>
    <step order="3">Thread the narrowing through `AgentToolCatalogProjector` (~:74–433) so non-advisory turns are unaffected.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify against ADR-039 MUST-NOTs: no classifier, no second intent-detection, no routing config outside the Binding table; the Text-path agent turn stays the sole decider.</step>
    <step order="5">Unit-test the projection with and without the allow-list (advisory turn mounts only allow-listed tools; non-advisory unaffected).</step>
    <step order="6">dotnet build + dotnet publish size check; record absolute size + delta; run the vulnerable-package scan.</step>
    <step order="7">/conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If scoping the allow-list cannot be expressed as deterministic pre-filtering and appears to need any capability-SELECTING logic (intent detection / routing / a second dispatch), STOP and escalate (ADR-039 forbids a second decider) rather than adding routing.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`AgentToolProjection.PreFilter` (~:123–187) + `AgentToolCatalogProjector` (~:74–433) already perform the sanctioned deterministic tool projection.</existing>
    <extension>Add a context-scoping predicate that narrows the mounted set to the Action's allow-list when advisory — no new surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without pre-filter narrowing, an advisory Action either mounts nothing or the whole catalog; the bounded grounded-recommend tier (task 012) cannot mount exactly its two tools without adding a forbidden second decider.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AgentToolProjection.cs (PreFilter allow-list narrowing predicate)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/AgentToolCatalogProjector.cs (narrowing threaded through)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ projection unit tests (with/without allow-list)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An advisory turn mounts ONLY the allow-listed grounded tools (via the deterministic pre-filter).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Non-advisory turns are unaffected by the narrowing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No classifier / second intent-detection / routing surface is added (negative case, verified against ADR-039 MUST-NOTs).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The single Text-path agent turn remains the sole probabilistic decider.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Projection unit test passes (with/without allow-list) in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size ≤60 MB reported (absolute + delta); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>The defining ADR-039 constraint of R4 lives here: bounded tool set = deterministic pre-filter narrowing, NEVER a second decider. Depends on task 010's opt-in field. Task 012 authors the advisory Action whose allow-list = {grid_overview, daily_briefing_overview}. /conflict-check with assistant-r3 + compose-r5/r6 before the PR.</notes>
